# Looking things up in SEED

Two MCP servers are declared in `.cursor/mcp.json` and travel with the repository. `seed-docs` needs
no credentials. `seed-figma` activates only when `FIGMA_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` is set.

SEED ships several packages that version independently and rename tokens between majors. Recall is
unreliable here; look it up.

## Reach for a tool when

| Question                                       | Tool                                               |
| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| Does a component for this exist?               | `list_react_components`                            |
| What props does it take?                       | `get_react_component({ componentName })`           |
| When should this component be used at all?     | `get_docs_component({ componentName })`            |
| What is the exact token name?                  | `get_rootage({ path: "/color.json" })`             |
| What is this component's spec?                 | `get_rootage({ path: "/components/<name>.json" })` |
| Which icon shows a left arrow?                 | `search_icons({ query: "화살표" })` — Korean works |
| How do I import that icon?                     | `get_icon_details({ iconName })`                   |
| How is theming or Tailwind meant to be set up? | `get_react_getting_started({ path })`              |
| What changed in the last release?              | `get_react_changelog`                              |

Call `discover_tools` once at the start of a session if you are unsure what is available.

## Offline fallbacks

If the MCP server is unavailable:

- `.seed/tokens.json` — the token catalog for the installed version, generated locally
- `.seed/llms/` — cached SEED documentation, refreshed by `pnpm seed:sync`
- `pnpm seed:docs <component>` — prints the doc, llms.txt and snippet URLs
- `https://seed-design.io/llms/react/components/<name>.txt` — fetch directly

## Keeping up with SEED

`pnpm seed:sync` regenerates `.seed/tokens.json`, `.cursor/rules/_generated-seed-tokens.mdc` and the
cached docs from the packages currently installed. `pnpm seed:compat` checks the vendored snippets in
`src/shared/seed/` against those package versions. CI runs both, so a dependency bump that leaves
them stale fails the build.

After bumping any `@seed-design/*` version:

1. `pnpm seed:sync`
2. `pnpm seed:compat` — if it complains, re-add the affected snippets with `pnpm seed:add ui:<name>`
3. `pnpm verify:lockin` — confirms the theme reset still removes Tailwind's own tokens
4. Read `get_react_changelog` for anything that moved
